WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.708
In simple terms, the mom skill gives your coding agent a review

00:00:04.708 --> 00:00:05.100
team.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.960
It lets other tools inspect a change before you ship it.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.460
One governor stays responsible for the final decision.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.720
Your agent is still the only writer and verifier.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.220
The name expands to Mixture of Model Modality.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.220
Say the short name like mom.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.760
It is not a new model.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.080
It is not a vote.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.840
Think of it as a group of inspectors.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.000
Different reviewer tools look at code, words and supported media.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Then they hand their untrusted claims back to one governor.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.080
AI can be fast and still miss an edge case.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.060
It can miss a security boundary.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.780
It can also give a confusing explanation.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.240
The mom skill makes challenge routine.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.960
A second inspector asks a different question.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.860
The governor checks the claim.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.800
Every decision stays inspectable.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.680
First, take a baseline.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.160
Next, send the scoped change to selected reviewers in parallel.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.943
Then investigate each material claim, like checking a receipt before

00:00:58.943 --> 00:00:59.900
reimbursing it.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.616
Fix only what the evidence supports, and write the decision,

00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:06.960
evidence and remaining uncertainty in a private audit notebook.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.240
Version 1.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.480
16 adds per-reviewer token and cost accounting, ratings and route

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.296
reliability, trusted guidance layers, split diffs with a separate

00:01:16.296 --> 00:01:20.112
quorum for each piece, parallel jobs, a capability-aware modality

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:23.928
registry, explicit update checks, opt-in retry for invalid output,

00:01:23.928 --> 00:01:27.320
and a shared Setup Center and ledger design.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.363
The governor is like the lead editor, project manager and referee in

00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:31.700
one.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.700
It is the only writer.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.680
It owns the final decision.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.560
Reviewer output is like sticky notes from inspectors.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.560
Useful, but never commands.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.080
Account logins are explicit and OAuth-based.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.540
Automatic updates stay off by default.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.480
On Windows, a planted git.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.120
exe or taskkill.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.340
exe in the reviewed project is never started.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.920
A claim is a proposition from a reviewer.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.620
It is not a fact yet.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.480
The governor reproduces it, or rejects it with evidence.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.356
The public record keeps those decisions, release-gate runs and

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.440
cross-platform checks.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.000
Think of it as a lab notebook.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.680
It is not a universal productivity or accuracy guarantee.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.000
More reviewers use more quota.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.820
Provider availability still varies.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.140
Use the public upgrade prompt.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.060
Verify the signed release and package before running new code.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.140
Keep the clone in a permanent folder, preview the plan, then approve

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:24.480
it.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.180
Existing users keep their harness scopes and private ledgers.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.040
Open the local Setup Center.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.430
Choose your current agent, sign in to a reviewer through its

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:38.022
official account flow, then verify the route with disclosed

00:02:38.022 --> 00:02:38.820
synthetic input.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.491
Start with one ready inspector; add others only when their

00:02:42.491 --> 00:02:43.960
perspective earns the quota.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.103
Back in the project, choose which providers may receive the scoped

00:02:48.103 --> 00:02:48.480
work.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.522
Ask the mom skill to review the changes, investigate findings,

00:02:52.522 --> 00:02:56.160
verify fixes, record every decision and show the ledger.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.300
Your agent coordinates; no reviewer edits your project.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.180
A valid review is not an acceptance badge.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.140
The governor quotes the claim.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.360
It reproduces the claim, or rejects it with evidence.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.980
Deferred work stays visible.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.472
Quorum is the minimum number of independent inspectors needed before

00:03:13.472 --> 00:03:14.520
a gate opens.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.100
Think of two signatures on a safety checklist.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.240
It is not a popularity vote.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.500
It never replaces judgment.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.859
The private ledger connects the input hash, reviewer responses,

00:03:25.859 --> 00:03:28.280
investigations, tests and final rulings.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.920
Think of it as an audit notebook.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.140
You can revisit it.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:31.960
You can explain it.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.720
You can hand it over.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.620
Your project and provider logs stay private.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.340
Use the mom skill on one meaningful change.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.380
Use it for a difficult decision.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.580
Use it for a release you want challenged.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.340
Start with the guide.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:45.880
Connect one reviewer.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.500
Judge the value on your own work.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.300
Version 1.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.940
16 is live at marroccofella.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.040
io/skills/momm/.
